      "id": "native-latency-size",
      "title": "Time against message size, host memory, Linux to Mac",
      "summary": "Line chart on logarithmic axes. Completion-confirmed TBCCL transfers from 4 KiB to 16 MiB take 126 microseconds at 4 KiB, 269 at 64 KiB, 1,118 at 1 MiB (range 779 to 1,480 over repetitions), 2,432 at 4 MiB and 8,669 at 16 MiB. Two further series are round trips of 64 byte and 4 KiB messages, about 128 microseconds, which are a different kind of measurement and not one-way latencies. Small and medium messages are latency- and variability-bound.",
      "conditions": "Host memory, TBCCL 0.6.0 over TCP/IPv4, direct Thunderbolt 4 link, MTU 9000. The two round-trip series are ping-pongs that include the return trip and are not halved; the completion-confirmed series times one transfer up to its acknowledgement. The three series have different timing semantics and are not a like-for-like comparison.",
      "page": "native-results.md",
      "section": [
